    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d708fab4_aaeea71b",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-11T23:08:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per our general state machine flow, it\u0027s designed to send a DiscMode for every SVID we received from DiscSVID.  So for example, if you have an Apple 3-in-1 dongle it will have both a DP SVID and also an Apple SVID.  The current flow iterates over these and sends a DiscMode for each, before entering DP mode. \n\nSo the dfp_discover_modes() function will just fill in the next SVID we received during discovery here.  This works if the only 2 received are the Intel SVID, but would not work otherwise.",
      "parentUuid": "437b20ca_1f692a04",
